  "question": {
    "text": "Based on the equation:\n$$\n\\Delta \\mathrm{E}=-2.0 \\times 10^{-18} \\mathrm{~J}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_2^2}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}_1^2}\\right)\n$$\nthe wavelength of the light that must be absorbed to excite hydrogen electron from level $n=1$ to level $\\mathrm{n}=2$ will be: $\\left(\\mathrm{h}=6.625 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}, \\mathrm{C}=3 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\right)$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$1.325 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$1.325 \\times 10^{-10} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$2.650 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$5.300 \\times 10^{-10} \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\Delta E=-2.0 \\times 10^{-18} \\times\\left(\\frac{1}{2^2}-\\frac{1}{1^2}\\right) \\\\\n&=-2.0 \\times 10^{-18} \\times \\frac{-3}{4} \\\\\n&=1.5 \\times 10^{-18} \\\\\n&\\Delta E=\\frac{h c}{\\lambda} \\\\\n&\\lambda=\\frac{h c}{\\Delta E}=\\frac{6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\times 3 \\times 10^8}{1.5 \\times 10^{-18}} \\\\\n&=1.325 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~m}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}